      "problem": "Which of the following diagrams shows the graph of $y={log}_{10}⁡x?$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's recall some of the basic properties of $y={log}_{10}⁡x:$\n\n- The domain is $x>0$, and the range is $-\\infty <y<\\infty .$\n\n- The graph has the vertical asymptote $x=0.$\n\n- The function is an increasing function.\n\n- The graph passes through the point $(1,0).$\n\n- For $x>1$, the graph is positive and grows very slowly as we increase $x.$ We say that $y\\to \\infty $ (slowly) as $x\\to \\infty .$\n\nOf the given functions, the only one that has all of these properties is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14245974/assets/5a52b4fcfb2cc410c894f69771ff450ceef1366048438345d1444e35186d9d76.png)",
